mode: "100644"
text: "# Content Mix — balance and variety\n\nA feed people follow has a through-line and a rhythm. This is how you build balance into a batch\ninstead of producing 30 disconnected posts (or 30 ads).\n\nA plan is organized along three axes: **pillars** (the themes), **intents** (the job each post\ndoes), and **formats** (the shape). Vary all three across the period.\n\n---\n\n## Pillars — the themes (the *what*)\n\n3–5 recurring themes the brand owns, drawn from `content-pillars` or derived from the brand\nprofile's positioning, audience, and point of view. Every post belongs to a pillar. Pillars\nkeep the feed coherent and make planning faster — you're filling known buckets, not inventing\nfrom scratch each time.\n\nSpread posts roughly evenly across pillars over the period so no single theme dominates (unless\na campaign justifies it).\n\n## Intents — the job each post does (the *why*)\n\nTag every post with one primary intent:\n\n- **Educate** — teach something useful (how-to, tips, breakdowns). High save value.\n- **Entertain** — make them feel something / smile (relatable, story, behind-the-scenes). High\n  reach/shareability.\n- **Inspire** — show what's possible (transformation, vision, customer wins).\n- **Connect** — build community (questions, opinions, shared identity, replies). High comments.\n- **Promote** — ask for the action (launch, offer, CTA-forward).\n\n**The ratio matters more than any single post.** Lead heavily with educate / entertain /\nconnect; keep **promote a clear minority** (a common working guideline is roughly 80% value &\nconnection, 20% promotion — adjust to the brand, but never invert it). A feed that only ever\nasks gets muted. Give a lot; ask a little.\n\n## Formats — the shape (rotate them)\n\nDon't run the same format every day. Rotate across what the platforms and brand support:\nsingle image, carousel, short video (Reel/TikTok/Short), text post, thread, story, behind-the-\nscenes. Match format to intent — how-tos work as carousels; stories and entertainment as video;\nhot takes as text. Rotating formats keeps the feed visually varied and reaches different\naudience preferences.\n\nAlso rotate **hook mechanisms** (via `hook-writer`) so openings don't all sound the same.\n\n## Recurring series — anchor the calendar\n\nBuild in one or two repeatable series — a weekly tip, a Friday behind-the-scenes, a monthly\ncustomer story. Series:\n\n- cut decision fatigue (the slot's purpose is pre-decided),\n- build audience habit and recognition,\n- make the calendar feel intentional, not random.\n\nLeave the rest of the calendar for timely and one-off posts.\n\n---\n\n## The mix anti-patterns\n\n- **All promotion** — the audience tunes out. Promotion rides on earned attention from value.\n- **All one format** — monotonous; caps reach to one audience preference.\n- **All one pillar** — narrow and repetitive; the brand looks one-note.\n- **All educational, never human** — competent but cold; connection content is what builds\n  loyalty.\n- **No series / all random** — exhausting to sustain and forgettable to follow.\n\n## A simple balanced week (illustrative)\n\nFor ~5 posts/week on one platform:\n\n1. **Educate** (carousel) — pillar A\n2. **Connect** (question) — pillar B\n3. **Entertain / story** (video) — pillar C\n4. **Inspire / proof** (image + caption) — pillar A\n5. **Promote** (the week's single ask) — pillar D\n\nFour give, one ask. Three formats. Four pillars. Scale the pattern up for a month; keep the\nratio.\n"
